Licences of the SRFI implementations under stdlib/srfi/
=======================================================

Each stdlib/srfi/<N>.scm names where its code came from in its header. Code
written for Turmeric is under Turmeric's own licence. Code taken from
elsewhere keeps its copyright notice there and its licence here
(docs/archive/r7rs-srfi-plan.md, D6).

File       From                                      Licence
---------  ----------------------------------------  -----------------------
1.scm      chibi-scheme lib/srfi/1.sld and the       BSD-3 (chibi, below)
           nine lib/srfi/1/*.scm files it includes
2.scm      chibi-scheme lib/srfi/2.sld               BSD-3 (chibi, below)
8.scm      SRFI 8's reference implementation         MIT (SRFI, below)
           Copyright (C) John David Stone (1999)
17.scm     SRFI 17's reference implementation        MIT (SRFI, below)
           (setter, set-setter!,
           getter-with-setter): Copyright (C) Per
           Bothner (2000).  Its table of standard
           setters is written for Turmeric
26.scm     SRFI 26's reference implementation,       public domain
           cut.scm (Al Petrofsky, adapted by
           Sebastian Egner)
27.scm     SRFI 27's reference implementation        MIT (SRFI, below)
           (srfi-27-reference/: mrg32k3a-a.scm,
           mrg32k3a.scm, the record type from
           srfi-27-a.scm): Copyright (C)
           Sebastian Egner (2002)
31.scm     SRFI 31's implementation                  MIT (SRFI, below)
           Copyright (C) Dr. Mirko Luedde (2002)
35.scm     SRFI 35's reference implementation        MIT (SRFI, below)
           Copyright (C) Richard Kelsey, Michael
           Sperber (2002)
41.scm     chibi-scheme lib/srfi/41.scm, its         BSD-3 (chibi, below);
           adaptation of SRFI 41's reference         the reference, MIT
           (Copyright (C) 2007 Philip L. Bewig)      (SRFI, below)
42.scm     SRFI 42's reference implementation,       MIT (SRFI, below)
           ec.scm: Copyright (C) Sebastian Egner
           (2003)
48.scm     SRFI 48's reference implementation, as    MIT (SRFI, below)
           the SRFI's repository carries it
           (test/srfi-48.scm): Copyright 2003
           Kenneth A Dickey, 2017 Hamayama
60.scm     SRFI 60's implementation as its document  MIT (SRFI, below)
           carries it (SLIB's logical.scm):
           Copyright (C) Aubrey Jaffer (2004, 2005)
64.scm     SRFI 64's R7RS implementation, from the   MIT (SRFI, below)
           SRFI's repository (contrib/taylan.kammer):
           Copyright (c) 2015 Taylan Kammer
78.scm     SRFI 78's reference implementation,       MIT (SRFI, below)
           check.scm: Copyright (c) 2005-2006
           Sebastian Egner

The files not listed (4, 6, 9, 11, 13, 14, 16, 23, 28, 30, 34, 38, 39, 45,
61, 66, 69, 87, 98, 216) are export lists, adaptors and implementations
written for Turmeric.

One test suite here is derived from an SRFI's own tests rather than chibi's:
tests/r7rs/srfi/216/tests.scm, from SRFI 216's srfi-216-tests.scm,
Copyright (C) 2020 Vladimir Nikishkin, MIT (SRFI, below).


